vars: {
  d2-config: {
    layout-engine: elk
    theme-id: 0
    pad: 24
  }
}

title: |||md
  # dl8 kernel relations
  Every kernel relation is a **function over bound arguments**,  
  never a stored  
  table, except the two snapshots. The checker refuses a call  
  whose bound  
  positions match no keyset (`_3_check/_4_mode.rs`). Source:  
  `v8/src/_6_eval/_4_kernel.rs`, tables  
  `v8/src/_2_lower/_9_kernel.rs`.  

  | color | meaning |
  |---|---|
  | green | builds a value |
  | amber | reads a stored table |
  | blue | tests, no value made |
  | magenta | the pull, demand() |

  flow: nil → cons → intern → snapshots next round; demand pulls  
  cons and intern per level; count switches demand off.  
|||
title.class: txt

direction: down

classes: {
  txt:   { style.font-color: "#1b1b1b"; style.fill: "#ffffff"; style.stroke: "#cccccc" }
  build: { style.fill: "#e6f4ea"; style.stroke: "#2e7d32"; style.font-color: "#1b3d1f" }
  table: { style.fill: "#fff3e0"; style.stroke: "#ef6c00"; style.font-color: "#3e2723" }
  test:  { style.fill: "#e3f2fd"; style.stroke: "#1565c0"; style.font-color: "#0d2a4a" }
  pull:  { style.fill: "#f3e5f5"; style.stroke: "#7b1fa2"; style.font-color: "#3a1046" }
}

kernels: {
  grid-columns: 3
  grid-gap: 40
  style.stroke: transparent
  style.fill: transparent
nil: "nil / 1" {
  class: build
  why: |||md
  **why** the empty list, the seed of every argument list.  

  **when** keyset `[]`: nothing needs binding, always runnable.  

  **dl7** `(nil ?Empty)`  
  **prolog** `proves(_, call(ref(kernel(nil)), [const([])])).`  
  **rust** `vec![vec![u.compound("const",  
  vec![u.empty_list()])]]`  
  |||
  why.class: txt
}

cons: "cons / 3   head tail list" {
  class: build
  why: |||md
  **why** one list cell at a time. The only structural  
  constructor, so nesting is lists of lists and every  
  walk is one `cons` per level.  

  **dl7** `(cons ?Source ?Empty ?Arguments)`  

  **when** two modes, checker picks by what is bound:  

  | keyset | bound | returns |
  |---|---|---|
  | `[0,1]` | head, tail | list |
  | `[2]` | list | head, tail |

  |||
  why.class: txt
  code: |`rust
  Kernel::Cons => {
    if let Some(list) = args[2] {
      // list bound: split const([H|T])
      let items = u.as_list(u.unary(list,"const")?)?;
      let head = items[0];
      let tail = u.compound("const",
                   vec![u.list(&items[1..])]);
      return vec![vec![head, tail, list]];
    }
    if let (Some(head), Some(tail)) = (args[0], args[1]) {
      // head+tail bound: build const([H|T])
      let mut items = u.as_list(u.unary(tail,"const")?)?;
      items.insert(0, head);
      let list = u.compound("const", vec![u.list(&items)]);
      return vec![vec![head, tail, list]];
    }
    vec![]
  }
  `|
}

intern: "intern / 3   ctor args return" {
  class: build
  why: |||md
  **why** canonical identity for an application. Two calls  
  with equal ctor and args give one `TermId`, so a type like  
  `(Partial User)` is one value everywhere. Every request is  
  also recorded as an output row for the next round.  

  **when** keyset `[0,1]`: ctor and args bound, return free.  

  **dl7** `(intern Partial ?Arguments ?Result)`  
  **prolog** `intern_value(ref(C), const(Tagged),  
  ref(application(C, Args)))`  
  |||
  why.class: txt
  code: |`rust
  Kernel::Intern => {
    let ctor = u.unary(ctor_tagged, "ref")?;
    let tagged = u.as_list(u.unary(arguments, "const")?)?;
    let plain: Vec<_> = tagged.iter()
      .map(|t| semantic(u, *t))       // strip ref/const
      .collect::<Option<_>>()?;
    let app = u.compound("application",
                vec![ctor, u.list(&plain)]);
    let result = u.compound("ref", vec![app]);
    vec![vec![ctor_tagged, arguments, result]]
  }
  `|
}

edge_ref: "edge_ref / 3   owner label return" {
  class: build
  why: |||md
  **why** name an edge as a value: `ref(edge(Owner, Label))`.  
  Lets a rule talk about a field itself, the way `(: Owner  
  label target)` declares it.  

  **when** keyset `[0,1]`: owner and label bound.  

  **surface** none. The lowerer emits it for a declaration  
  whose label is an expression, e.g. `(: (Key "account" O)  
  int)`.  
  |||
  why.class: txt
  code: |`rust
  Kernel::EdgeRef => {
    let owner = u.unary(owner_tagged, "ref")?;
    let sem = semantic(u, label)?;
    let edge = u.compound("edge", vec![owner, sem]);
    let result = u.compound("ref", vec![edge]);
    vec![vec![owner_tagged, label, result]]
  }
  `|
}

snapshots: "intern_snapshot / 3  and  edge_snapshot / 4" {
  class: table
  why: |||md
  **why** the backward doors. `intern` and the graph only  
  build forward. A rule that starts from a `Result` and wants  
  its arguments, or from a type and wants its fields, reads  
  a stored copy of the previous round instead.  

  **when** scanned like any table, any binding works.  
  Edge keys: `[0,1]` by name, `[0,3]` by position.  

  **dl7**  
  `(intern_snapshot Partial ?Arguments ?Result)`  
  `(edge_snapshot ?Owner ?Name ?Target ?Index)`  

  **filled by** comptime rounds, `_4_comptime/_2_rounds.rs`,  
  from every `intern` output row and every `:` edge.  
  |||
  why.class: txt
}

int: "int_lt int_le int_eq int_ne int_ge int_gt / 2" {
  class: test
  why: |||md
  **why** integer comparison. A test, no value produced.  

  **when** keyset `[0,1]`: both sides bound and integer.  
  Under `not`, the complement holds (`negative_holds`).  

  **dl7** `(int_lt ?Prior ?Index)`  
  |||
  why.class: txt
  code: |`rust
  Kernel::Int(cmp) => match int_pair(u, args) {
    Some((l, r)) if cmp.holds(l, r) =>
      vec![vec![args[0].unwrap(), args[1].unwrap()]],
    _ => vec![],
  }
  `|
}

count: "count in a head" {
  class: test
  why: |||md
  **why** an aggregate over a closed stratum. Runs after  
  every lower rule has stopped, so it sees the full table.  

  **when** the body is evaluated with `tables_only = true`,  
  which switches `demand()` off inside it.  
  |||
  why.class: txt
  code: |`lisp
  (<- (key_rank ?Source ?SourceIndex (count ?PriorIndex))
      (keyed_edge ?Source ?Name ?Opts ?Target ?SourceIndex)
      (key_predecessor ?Source ?SourceIndex ?PriorIndex))
  `|
}

demand: "demand()   the one pull in a push engine" {
  class: pull
  why: |||md
  **why** bottom-up rounds fill tables from facts. A body goal  
  like `(Partial ?User ?R)` with `?User` already bound has no  
  table row yet in round 0. `demand` runs the rules for that  
  head with the bound pattern, top-down, memoized per  
  `(rel, pattern)`, and hands the rows back unstored.  

  **when** all four clauses hold.  
  |||
  why.class: txt
  code: |`rust
  let demand = !self.tables_only        // outside aggregates
    && kernel.is_none()                 // a derived rel
    && pattern.iter().any(|t| t.is_some()) // one arg bound
    && self.rules_by_rel.contains_key(&goal.rel);
  if demand {
    solutions.extend(self.demand(goal.rel, &pattern));
  }
  `|
}
}
